Meridian Electronics — AI Customer Support Platform
This repository contains a production-ready AI-powered customer support system for Meridian Electronics. The platform enables users to check product availability, manage orders, and handle account inquiries through a secure, tool-augmented conversational agent.

Beyond a simple chatbot, this system demonstrates robust AI orchestration, safety guardrails, infrastructure automation, and observability best practices.

Core Capabilities
Intelligent Query Enhancement
User queries are not passed directly to the model. Instead, they are pre-processed and enhanced to improve clarity, completeness, and tool alignment.

Contextual Expansion: Expands vague or underspecified queries into structured intents using conversation history.

Intent Refinement: Normalizes user input for consistent agent behavior and fixes typos.

Implementation: backend/utils/prompt_enhancer.py

AI Orchestration & Tooling
The system uses a LangGraph-based ReAct agent to dynamically reason about user requests and invoke backend tools via the Model Context Protocol (MCP).

Dynamic Tool Selection: Automatically loads and selects tools based on user intent.

Strict Grounding: The agent is strictly instructed to rely on internal tools for inventory and pricing to prevent hallucinations.

Implementation: backend/graph/mcp_agent.py

MCP Integration
The agent connects to internal services via a streaming MCP endpoint, decoupling AI logic from business systems.

Transport: Supports real-time tool execution via Server-Sent Events (SSE).

Configuration: Target URL defined via MCP_SERVER_URL.

Implementation: backend/graph/mcp_agent.py (utilizing streamablehttp_client)

Guardrails & Safety
A multi-layered guardrail system ensures reliability, security, and professional behavior.

Input Guardrails
Injection Protection: Scans for common prompt injection patterns (e.g., "ignore previous instructions") and blocks malicious overrides.

Implementation: backend/utils/guardrails.py (check_for_prompt_injection)

Output Guardrails
Leakage Prevention: Scans for and redacts sensitive data like OpenAI API keys or internal system prompts.

Professional Tone: Filters forbidden phrases to maintain a customer-safe tone.

Implementation: backend/utils/guardrails.py (apply_output_guardrails)

Execution Constraints
Timeout Protection: A 60-second timeout prevents "hanging" processes during complex tool calls.

Recursion Limit: Prevents infinite loops in agent reasoning (limit set to 5 steps).

Observability & Monitoring
Designed for production-grade visibility into performance, cost, and reliability.

Structured Logging: Uses a dedicated Meridian_Support_Engine logger to capture connection status, agent steps, and errors.

Latency Tracking: Middleware calculates processing time for every request and injects an X-Process-Time header.

Token & Cost Monitoring: Tracks token consumption per user and logs metadata for LLM cost analysis.

Health Checks: Root endpoint (/) provides instant service health validation.

Implementation: backend/main.py (Middleware) and backend/graph/mcp_agent.py (Token tracking)

Infrastructure & Deployment
Containerization
Dockerized Stack: Separate Dockerfiles for frontend and backend, optimized for cross-platform builds.

Automation: deploy.sh automates the build and push process to Amazon ECR.

Terraform (Infrastructure as Code)
AWS Provisioning: Manages ECR repositories, IAM roles, and AWS App Runner services.

Implementation: terraform/main.tf

Configuration
Environment Variables: Managed via backend/config.py and provisioned in App Runner for secure runtime access.

Testing Strategy
A comprehensive test suite ensures both correctness and resilience.

Agent Tests: Validate tool loading and reasoning logic using mock connections.

API Tests: Ensure endpoint health and correct handling of environment configurations.

Implementation: backend/tests/

Run tests:

Bash
cd backend
pytest tests/ -v


Comprehensive Evaluation
Beyond isolated unit tests, the system includes an automated evaluation pipeline to score the AI agent against real-world customer scenarios and ensure it strictly adheres to Meridian Electronics' business logic.

The evaluation suite (backend/evaluation.py) tests the live agent against a predefined dataset of:

Happy Paths: Core workflows like inventory lookup and order status checks.

Customer Authentication: Ensuring the agent correctly parses emails and PINs to retrieve sensitive account data.

Edge Cases: Handling missing parameters gracefully (e.g., asking for an order ID instead of hallucinating one) and clarifying vague product requests.

Out of Bounds & Adversarial: Verifying the agent refuses non-technical questions and strictly resists prompt injection attempts to leak its system prompt.

Run the evaluation:

Bash
cd backend
uv run evaluation.py